f human bacterial pathogens, turned 100 this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/08/science/bacteria-library-nctc.html', 'snippet': 'Britain’s National Collection of Type Cultures, a library of human bacterial pathogens, turned 100 this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the winter of 1915, Pvt. Ernest Cable arrived at the Number 14 Stationary Hospital in Wimereux, France, in bad shape. The British army’s soldiers stationed on the Western Front of World War I were being ravaged by a variety of microscopic enemies. For Private Cable, it was Shigella flexneri, the bacterium that causes dysentery.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/science/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/09/science/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 717}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/science/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 857, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/science/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1714, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/science/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri/00SCI-BACTERIA-flexneri-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/09/science/00SCI-BAC