ard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/us/09ambriefing-defund/09ambriefing-defund-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Defund’ Conundrum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-06-09T10:39:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e302f0f-d654-5f03-9eba-e3088719c4d8', 'word_count': 1615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e302f0f-d654-5f03-9eba-e3088719c4d8'}, {'abstract': 'In her debut as a director, the actress Maryam Zaree explores her birth at an infamous Iranian prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/09/movies/born-in-evin-review.html', 'snippet': 'In her debut as a director, the actress Maryam Zaree explores her birth at an infamous Iranian prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Born in Evin,” the German actress Maryam Zaree says that she’s tired of playing television clichés of Middle Eastern refugees fleeing from “made-up horrors.” She wants to tell the story of the real horrors that she and her parents fled in the 1980s in Iran, where Zaree was born in the notorious Evin Prison for political dissidents. The problem is she has no memories of that time — and her parents refuse to speak of it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/03/arts/borni