g media outlets and cracking down on the opposition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — President Pierre Nkurunziza of Burundi died of heart failure on Monday just weeks after a crucial election to choose a successor to replace him after 15 years of autocratic rule over the Central African nation. He was 55.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/world/09burundi/09burundi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/09/world/09burundi/09burundi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/world/09burundi/09burundi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/world/09burundi/09burundi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/world/09burundi/09burundi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/09/world/09burundi/09burundi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/09/world/09burundi/09burundi-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'President of Burundi, Pierre Nkurunziza, 55, Dies of Heart Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Who Ruled  Burundi With Iron Fist  For 15 Years Dies at 55', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nkurunziza, Pierre', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Burundi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-09T15:49:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abdi Latif Dahir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abdi', 'middlename': 'Latif', 'lastname': 'Dahir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/755f1690-9c51-53e9-9760-f37b2fb89356', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/755f1690-9c51-53e9-9760-f37b2fb89356'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Dani García plans his restaurant for later this year, pizza for delivery and takeout in Park Slope, Brooklyn, and more restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/09/dining/nyc-restaurant-news-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Dani García plans his restaurant for later this year, pizza for delivery and takeout in Park Slope, Brooklyn, and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Spanish chef Dani García once had a presence in New York, at Manzanilla on Park Avenue South. It lasted a year. Now, Mr. García, whose restaurant, Dani García in Marbella, Spain, held three Michelin stars before it closed last year, is coming back to Manhattan. His latest effort, Casa Dani, will be one of two fine-dining destinations at Citizens, a 40,000-square-foot space being designed by David Rockwell in the Manhattan West complex by Brookfield Properties and scheduled to open around the end of the year. (The fine-dining restaurant is Katsuya, from the Los Angeles-based sushi chef Katsuya Uechi.) In addition, Mr. Garcia will open a fast-casual restaurant, Minük, in a food hall component of Citizens. The Citizens project’s formal and casual restaurants are all owned by C3, a subsidiary of SBE, a global hospitality company founded by Sam Nazarian. C3’s other brands include Umami Burger, Krispy Rice, Sam’s Crispy Chicken and Plant Nation.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/10/dining/09OFF/09OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 563, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/10/dining/09OFF/09OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 563}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/10/dining/09OFF/09OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/10/dining/09OFF/09OFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1921, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/10/dining/09OFF/09OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/10/dining/09OFF/09OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/10/dining/09OFF/09OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Casa Dani, From a Michelin Chef, to Open in Manhattan West', 'kicker': 