 Bell’s “Inappropriate.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/09/books/review/noah-van-sciver-complete-works-of-fante-bukowski-gebrielle-bell-inappropriate.html', 'snippet': 'In his Graphic Content column, Ed Park reviews Noah Van Sciver’s “The Complete Works of Fante Bukowski” and Gabrielle Bell’s “Inappropriate.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A book about a fictitious writer includes, in its pages, a glowing New York Times review of said author by an equally fake reviewer, one “Trilly Stein.” Must a real-life Times reviewer take the bait? (A: Yes.) That Stein visits the same hooker as the made-up writer is just one of the gags in Noah Van Sciver’s graphic-novel omnibus THE COMPLETE WORKS OF FANTE BUKOWSKI (Fantagraphics, 452 pp., $39.99). As literary satires go, it’s both gleefully malicious and unrepentantly stupid — a winning combination, for the most part. Even my colleague Trilly Stein would laugh.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/05/books/review/VanSciver/VanSciver-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/05/books/review/VanSciver/VanSciver-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/05/books/review/VanSciver/VanSciver-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/05/books/review/VanSciver/VanSciver-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1673, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/05/books/review/VanSciver/VanSciver-thumbStandar