ported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a74d9a65-4af6-549b-a586-d577b8e69fc6', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a74d9a65-4af6-549b-a586-d577b8e69fc6'}, {'abstract': 'As lockdowns and quarantines stretch on, reports of child care facility closures have been coming in from coast to coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/10/parenting/virus-day-care-bright-horizons.html', 'snippet': 'As lockdowns and quarantines stretch on, reports of child care facility closures have been coming in from coast to coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The email arrived on a Thursday in mid-April, alerting parents that the Bright Horizons day care center in the Westwood neighborhood of Los Angeles would close the following Monday. The center had been a designated hub for essential workers since the beginning of the coronavirus pandemic in March, and it was a convenient site for physicians who worked at the nearby hospital. Its sudden closure left families with just a few days to find replacement child care, according to interviews with several of the parents affected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/04/multimedia/04-bright-horizons/04-bright-horizons-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/04/multimedia/04-bright-horizons/04-bright-horizons-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/04/multimedia/04-bright-horizons/04-bright-horizons-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/04/multimedia/04-bright-hori