'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-photojournalism', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-10T21:08:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chang W. Lee and Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chang', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51117067-904a-5f80-bbb9-af5ab15df31a', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51117067-904a-5f80-bbb9-af5ab15df31a'}, {'abstract': 'Essential reading from T’s archive, including pieces on how L.G.B.T.Q. culture has re-envisioned the worlds of food, art and entertainment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/10/t-magazine/pride-month-reading-list.html', 'snippet': 'Essential reading from T’s archive, including pieces on how L.G.B.T.Q. culture has re-envisioned the worlds of food, art and entertainment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stonewall was a riot. This has become the de facto slogan to describe the series of early-summer 1969 demonstrations that took place in front of New York City’s Stonewall Inn, the gay bar that became a battleground for the movement that catalyzed L.G.B.T.Q. rights in this country. Indeed, this historic rebellion is the reason we celebrate Pride Month each June. But as America rages on — against an uncured pandemic as well as its aftereffects, and for justice following the deaths of George Floyd, Breonna Taylor and others at the hands of police — that phrase, “Stonewall was a riot,” has taken on new resonance: It’s an assertion that fighting, not partying, is the root of our story. And this year, as many join in protests chanting “Black lives matter,” we are reminded that the Stonewall liberation was led by trans women of color, including Marsha P. Johnson and Sylvia Rivera, two activists whom city officials decided last year to honor with a monument, after decades of progress being too often attributed to mostly white gay men.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/t-magazine/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-copy/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/05/t-magazine/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-copy/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/t-magazine/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-copy/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/t-magazine/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-copy/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 1364, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/05/t-magazine/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-copy/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/05/t-magazine/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-copy/05tmag-revisionists-slide-59EV-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumb