ning the past, worried about the present and fearful of what comes next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brendan Hermanson, 51, a construction worker for three decades, has come through the pandemic healthy and employed. At home in Milwaukee, where he lives with his grown son, he tries to tune out the hostile politics in the country and wonders if he should bother to vote again for President Trump in November or “sit back and watch it crumble.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/11/us/politics/11unrest-voters/merlin_173322864_246e7cf4-65ae-4d93-9f19-d25c61bf288a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/11/us/politics/11unrest-voters/merlin_173322864_246e7cf4-65ae-4d93-9f19-d25c61bf288a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/11/us/politics/11unrest-voters/merlin_173322864_246e7cf4-65ae-4d93-9f19-d25c61bf288a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/11/us/politics/11unrest-voters/merlin_173322864_246e7cf4-65ae-4d93-9f19-d25c61bf288a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/11/us/politics/11unrest-voters/11unrest-voters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/11/us/politics/11unrest-voters/11unrest-voters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheig