 The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/020a9d3d-b280-51b7-aff9-1047d387dd97', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/020a9d3d-b280-51b7-aff9-1047d387dd97'}, {'abstract': 'We thought the U.S. presidential race would be the biggest story of the year. How wrong we were.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/12/podcasts/daily-newsletter-georgia-politics-education.html', 'snippet': 'We thought the U.S. presidential race would be the biggest story of the year. How wrong we were.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday’s episode, we spoke with Astead Herndon, a national political reporter, about the logistical meltdown in Georgia’s primary election. Astead was a regular guest on our series The Field, taking us with him on the campaign trail earlier this year. We asked him to reflect on what has changed since his last appearance for that show:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/11/opinion/11DAILY-newsletter/11DAILY-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/11/opinion/11DAILY-newsletter/11DAILY-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/11/opinion/11DAILY-newsletter/11DAILY-newsletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/11/opinion/11DAILY-newsletter/11DAILY-newsletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 