'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disease Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-13T09:27:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Wang and Elaine Yu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01dcdac4-55d1-5466-bd3a-d076d2dfa885', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01dcdac4-55d1-5466-bd3a-d076d2dfa885'}, {'abstract': 'There are about a septillion stars in the observable universe. You can bring a fraction into your home — which is more than enough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/13/at-home/coronavirus-create-your-own-night-sky.html', 'snippet': 'There are about a septillion stars in the observable universe. You can bring a fraction into your home — which is more than enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By now, you’ve spent more than enough time inside, and although you may be trying to get back out into nature, the options are still limited, especially after sunset. If you have a backyard or balcony and a clear moonless night, you might be able to look up and glimpse a few stars. But with the effects of light pollution, if you want to really see the stars — and lots of them — you’ll need to bring them to you.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/multimedia/14AH-STARS/14AH-STARS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType':