ype': 'article', 'news_desk': 'AtHome', 'section_name': 'At Home', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Dowd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cc8ca7b-274f-5a06-8aa4-d95360675b03', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cc8ca7b-274f-5a06-8aa4-d95360675b03'}, {'abstract': 'This June has restored the spirit of protest to Pride celebrations. Here are shows to help you understand the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/13/arts/5-pride-BLM-podcasts.html', 'snippet': 'This June has restored the spirit of protest to Pride celebrations. Here are shows to help you understand the moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, Pride has been forced back to its roots. Instead of celebrities waving from floats sponsored by TD Bank and Absolut Vodka, pandemic-masked protesters are marching in the streets demanding justice for black lives. Rainbow flags have been replaced with signs with the names of those killed by the police, like Tony McDade, a black trans man in Tallahassee, Fla. These protests may be perhaps the most genuine honoring of Pride, an annual commemoration of the 1969 Stonewall uprising, in which black and brown L.G.B.T.Q. people were a driving force. There is much to learn this Pride, and a legion of queer voices in podcasting can help you gain insight, find representation and feel comfort during this time. Here are a few of our recommendations.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2024, 'width': 2032, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO/14PRIDE-PODCASTS-COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '5 Podcasts at the Intersection of Pride Month and the Black Lives Matter Movement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Join Pride and #BLM By Listening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'QueerWOC (Radio Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Nancy (Radio Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N