Sammy Sosa revisit the home run record chase of 1998, and the dark detective drama returns to Netflix.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/14/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday-30-for-30-and-marcella.html', 'snippet': 'Mark McGwire and Sammy Sosa revisit the home run record chase of 1998, and the dark detective drama returns to Netflix.', 'lead_paragraph': '30 FOR 30: LONG GONE SUMMER 9 p.m. on ESPN. During the summer of 1998, many sports fans seemed to be captivated by one single story — the chase between the St. Louis Cardinals’ Mark McGwire and the Chicago Cubs’ Sammy Sosa to beat Roger Maris’s record of 61 home runs in a single season. In this documentary, Sosa and McGwire take viewers back to the high-drama slugfest. The film also explores how the revelations of steroid use in the league would later call the accomplishments of the sport —\xa0and that season —\xa0into question.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14tvcol-long/14tvcol-long-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14tvcol-long/14tvcol-long-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14tvcol-long/14tvcol-long-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14tvcol-long/14tvcol-long-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/arts/14tvcol-long/14tvco