ginal': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb4f9ba7-5529-53d3-aa2d-96d045a6eef3', 'word_count': 1305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb4f9ba7-5529-53d3-aa2d-96d045a6eef3'}, {'abstract': 'Its new report, “The Virus: What Went Wrong?,” recounts the progress of the disease and asks what America missed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/15/arts/television/review-frontline.html', 'snippet': 'Its new report, “The Virus: What Went Wrong?,” recounts the progress of the disease and asks what America missed.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Virus: What Went Wrong?,” a 90-minute installment of PBS’s “Frontline” premiering Tuesday, resurfaces the story of the pandemic that felt like an inescapable catastrophe just three weeks ago. Making no mention of protests or police, it’s like a courier with an urgent message who lost his place in line.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/15/arts/15frontline/15frontline-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/15/arts/15frontline/15frontline-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/15/arts/15frontline/15frontline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/15/arts/15frontline/15frontline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1459, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'l