d_paragraph': 'Would you like to own a set of six crystal Bar Hemingway martini glasses from the Ritz in Paris? At an auction from Sunday through Tuesday of tableware and other artifacts from the hotel, there are four lots of these, estimated at 400 to 600 euros (around $450 to $680). Or if your dining area lacks a silver-trimmed tableside gueridon from which to serve the pepperoni pie just delivered from the local pizzeria, there are those, too. The auction is live and online; the digital catalog of nearly 1,500 lots provides the window-shopping, along with a history of the hotel.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/15burner-ritz/15burner-ritz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/15burner-ritz/15burner-ritz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/15burner-ritz/15burner-ritz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/15burner-ritz/15burner-ritz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1464, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/15burner-ritz/15burner-ritz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/15burner-ritz/15burner-ritz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/15burner-ritz/15burner-ritz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Own a Piece of the Ritz', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Bid: Own a Piece Of the Ritz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Artcurial', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hotel Ritz Paris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-15T22:07:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8975e50-ff36-5915-8d09-a431006348f3', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8975e50-ff36-5915-8d09-a431006348f3'}, {'abstract': 'The poet Claudia Rankine writes for the Book Review about the climate in America at this moment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/15/books/review/claudia-rankine-weather-poem-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'The poet Claudia Rankine writes for the Book Review about the climate in America at this moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, the Book Review asked two prominent American poets to write original poems responding to this historic moment in our country. Claudia Rankine, whose poem “Weather” appears here and on the front cover of the June 21 issue, is the author of “Citizen: An American Lyric” and other collections, as well as two plays and various essays. She teaches at Yale. Her new book, “Just Us: An American Conversation,” will be published in September. Jericho Brown’s third volume of poetry, “The Tradition,” won the 2020 Pulitzer Prize for poetry. His poem “Say Thank You Say I’m Sorry” appears on the back page of the issue.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/books/review/16RankineWeather/merlin_169244583_b30977bd-fd33-47bd-b2d1-ecf3b4355a0e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/16/books/review/16RankineWeather/merlin_169244583_b30977bd-fd33-47bd-b2d1-ecf3b4355a0e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/books/review/16RankineWeather/merlin_169244583_b30977bd-fd33-47bd-b2d1-ecf3b4355a0e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/books/review/16RankineWeather/merlin_169244583_b30977bd-fd33-47bd-b2d1-ecf3b4355a0e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/books/review/16RankineWeather/16RankineWeather-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/16/books/review/16RankineWeather/16RankineWeather-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/books/revi