ndard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/16/briefing/16ambriefing-euro-promo/16ambriefing-euro-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/briefing/16ambriefing-euro-promo/16ambriefing-euro-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Tuesday Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-06-16T04:02:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabella Kwai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabella', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kwai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/447936d4-258f-5807-86b8-57888276d5aa', 'word_count': 1607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447936d4-258f-5807-86b8-57888276d5aa'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary on the 1992 Los Angeles riots airs on ABC, and Pop TV debuts an animated “One Day at a Time” special.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/16/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday-let-it-fall-and-one-day-at-a-time.html', 'snippet': 'A documentary on the 1992 Los Angeles riots airs on ABC, and Pop TV debuts an animated “One Day at a Time” special.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LET IT FALL: LOS ANGELES 1982-1992 (2017) 8 p.m. on ABC; stream on Netflix. This documentary by the director John Ridley (“American Crime”) was released on the 25th anniversary of the 1992 Los Angeles riots. ABC is resurfacing it — with a new introduction by John Legend — as police brutality and institutional racism consume the nation following the death of George Floyd. The movie traces the decade leading up to the riots, a response to a verdict that acquitted four police officers of assault for the beating of Rodney King. Ridley argues that King’s case was the straw that broke the camel’s back in a city rife with political and racial tensions. He backs his claim with nuance, interviewing retired police officials, witnesses and victims and perpetrators of violence. In her review for The New York Times, Jeannette Catsoulis named the movie a Critic’s Pick, calling it “wrenchingly humane.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/arts/16tvcol-letit/16tvcol-letit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 297, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/16/arts/16tvcol-letit/16tvcol-letit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 297}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/arts/16tvcol-letit/16tvcol-letit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 506, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/arts/16tvcol-letit/16tvcol-letit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1012, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/arts/16tvcol-letit/16tvcol-letit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/16/arts/16tvcol-letit/16tvcol-letit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/16/arts/16tvcol-letit/16tvcol-letit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday: ‘Let It Fall’ and ‘One Day at a Time’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-16T05:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Aridi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aridi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41559a97-7bf5-5b8b-814b-81c1e808f074', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41559a97-7bf5-5b8b-814b-81c1e808f074'}, {'abstract': 'The destruction of the office was a message aimed at President Moon Jae-in of South Korea, who had brokered failed talks between the North and the Trump administration. But it was also a message for Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/16/world/asia/north-korea-explosion-liaison-office.html', 'snippet': 'The destruction of the office was a message aimed at President Moon Jae-in of South Korea, who had brokered failed talks between the North and the Trump administration. But it was also a message for Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The North Korean warning aimed at South Korea has steadily been escalating in intensity for more than a year: Your matchmaking diplomacy between our leader and President Trump is failing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '\u200bNorth Korea’s Wrecking of Liaison Office a ‘Deat