sh-style barbecue in Chelsea Market, a roundup of steaks for delivery, and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amir Nathan, who worked at Via Carota and Maison Premiere, and his partner at this new takeout and delivery spot, the chef Jordan Anderson, who cooked at Maison Premiere and Olmsted, are making and delivering food from Maracuja, a bar and restaurant in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, that closed during the pandemic. The owners of Maracuja are their partners. “They were closed, so we were able to make a deal with them,” Mr. Nathan said. The food is Mediterranean with Middle Eastern influences. Spreads like baba ganoush, a lentil salad with fava beans, spicy carrots with harissa, roasted cauliflower with a pastrami rub, moussaka and bouillabaisse are some of the specialties. They also do picnic baskets. The project takes its name from an old Arab-Israeli television series. Mr. Nathan, who is from Israel, said he’d wanted to open a wine bar and grocery using that name for years, but the virus derailed those plans. The partners have not shelved their plans for a restaurant.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/16OFF/merlin_173469258_50eaff5b-fe66-4cc1-8940-be6089efb1bd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/16OFF/merlin_173469258_50eaff5b-fe66-4cc1-8940-be6089efb1bd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/16OFF/merlin_173469258_50eaff5b-fe66-4cc1-8940-be6089efb1bd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/16OFF/merlin_173469258_50eaff5b-fe66-4cc1-8940-be6089efb1bd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/16OFF/merlin_173469258_50eaff5b-fe66-4cc1-8940-be6089efb1bd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/16OFF/merlin_173469258_50eaff5b-fe66-4cc1-8940-be6089efb1bd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/16OFF/merlin_173469258_50eaff5b-fe66-4cc1-8940-be6089efb1bd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sami & Susu Opens for Takeout in Williamsburg', 'kicker': 'off the menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delivery Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-16T16:27:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a66d9699-7e0b-5881-a213-f24f3d52eea4', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a66d9699-7e0b-5881-a213-f24f3d52eea4'}, {'abstract': 'Reopening may be a long way off, but bar regulars have reassembled outdoors, and owners are trying to balance business and safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/16/dining/drinks/outdoor-bars-nyc-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Reopening may be a long way off, but bar regulars have reassembled outdoors, and owners are trying to balance business and safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tony Auliano and his wife, Melinda Lantz, stood, drinks in hand, outside the Factory 380, an Andy Warhol-themed bar on Third Avenue in Manhattan, on a recent Friday night. Mr. Auliano, 63, would have rather have been inside the bar, which, like many in New York City these days, is selling drinks to go. But he was happy for any social interaction he could get.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/17nybars5/17nybars5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/17nybars5/17nybars5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/17nybars5/17nybars5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/17nybars5/17nybars5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/17nybars5/17nybars5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/17/dining/17nybars5/17nybars5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank'