ight have shifted from I.C.U.s to wards where the sickest patients relearn how to walk and eat without choking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charlie Blueweiss, 33, woke up believing he was in a secret infirmary in an airport somewhere, maybe in China. He was certain someone was stalking him; threatening messages seemed to keep appearing on screens around him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/15/nyregion/00nyvirus-recovery/00nyvirus-recovery-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/15/nyregion/00nyvirus-recovery/00nyvirus-recovery-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/15/nyregion/00nyvirus-recovery/00nyvirus-recovery-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/15/nyregion/00nyvirus-recovery/00nyvirus-recovery-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/15/nyregion/00nyvirus-recovery/00nyvirus-recovery-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/15/nyregion/00nyvirus-recovery/00nyvirus-recovery-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/15/nyregion/00nyvirus-recovery/00nyvirus-recovery-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘When Am I Coming Home?’: A Tough Month Inside a Virus Recovery Unit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Some of the Sickest, Relearning to Walk or to Eat Without Choking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York-Presbyterian Hospital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ventilators (Medical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-17T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a8837c6-849e-56fa-8372-110f8b1a4d84', 'word_count': 1374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a8837c6-849e-56fa-8372-110f8b1a4d84'}, {'abstract': 'In a series of videos, the choreographer Alonzo King instructs performers to play with the natural world. “Let’s use the wind instead of ignoring it.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/17/arts/dance/alonzo-king-lines.html', 'snippet': 'In a series of videos, the choreographer Alonzo King instructs performers to play with the natural world. “Let’s use the wind instead of ignoring it.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choreographer Alonzo King has reached a point where he has no choice: He does what he does. “You keep pushing out beauty, you keep pushing out truth,” he said in a phone interview. “Of course, it’s a challe