n children are pressed into giving blood samples to build a sweeping genetic database that will add to Beijing’s growing surveillance capabilities, raising questions about abuse and privacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/17/world/asia/China-DNA-surveillance.html', 'snippet': 'Even children are pressed into giving blood samples to build a sweeping genetic database that will add to Beijing’s growing surveillance capabilities, raising questions about abuse and privacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police in China are collecting blood samples from men and boys from across the country to build a genetic map of its roughly 700 million males, giving the authorities a powerful new tool for their emerging high-tech surveillance state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Is Collecting DNA From Tens of Millions of Men and Boys, Using U.S. Equipment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Puts All Its Men in DNA Surveillance Net', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thermo Fisher Scientific Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'