ng', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cecilia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f478f890-fe1c-5590-8e16-591f6ba12089', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f478f890-fe1c-5590-8e16-591f6ba12089'}, {'abstract': 'Gabrielle Hamilton’s recipe is laborious work, but may just transport you to those bistros and hamburger stands you miss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/17/dining/its-time-for-french-fries.html', 'snippet': 'Gabrielle Hamilton’s recipe is laborious work, but may just transport you to those bistros and hamburger stands you miss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Is sourdough still trending, people all over the place nurturing starters, putting them to use in boules and baguettes, in pancakes and waffles? It sure seems that way, from the mail that I get. I think it’s because so many of us are still at home a lot, still working from the desk in the corner or not working from the couch in the living room, working the phone in search of unemployment insurance. With more time at home than usual, there’s more time to ferment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-eat/16mag-eat-articleLarge.png', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-eat/16mag-eat-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-eat/16mag-eat-jumbo.png', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-eat/16mag-eat-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1540, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-eat/16mag-eat-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-eat/16mag-eat-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/16/magazine/16mag-eat/16mag-eat-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Time for French Fries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-17T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c64a9a05-b4cc-5e71-aeb8-83b0c9cb1c51', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c64a9a05-b4cc-5e71-aeb8-83b0c9cb1c51'}, {'abstract': 'An online event will include his dance “Come Ye,” inspired by Nina Simone and Fela Kuti, artists for whom creativity and politics were inextricably linked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/17/arts/dance/ronald-k-brown-jacobs-pillow-award.html', 'snippet': 'An online event will include his dance “Come Ye,” inspired by Nina Simone and Fela Kuti, artists for whom creativity and politics were inextricably linked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival was canceled this summer for the first time in its history but that hasn’t stopped the festival’s organizers from handing out its annual award. This year’s recipient: Ronald K. Brown. Mr. Brown, an acclaimed choreographer whose work blends contemporary dance forms with West African and Caribbean influences, will be celebrated at a free online event on Saturday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/17ronbrown-item1/02LISTINGS-DANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/17ronbrown-item1/02LISTINGS-DANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/17ronbrown-item1/02LISTINGS-DANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/17ronbrown-item1/02LISTINGS-DANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/17ronbrown-item1/02LISTINGS-DANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/17ronbrown-item1/02LISTINGS-DANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/17ronbrown-item1/02LIST