: 'Bolton, John R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Mary L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Room Where It Happened: A White House Memoir (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Too Much And Never Enough: How My Family Created the World's Most Dangerous Man (Book)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Michael D (1966- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-17T16:12:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3cb31d6-7d81-5f83-9bd0-e9a5a19b9f57', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3cb31d6-7d81-5f83-9bd0-e9a5a19b9f57'}, {'abstract': 'People want to talk about the new normal, but there isn’t one yet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/17/at-home/newsletter.html', 'snippet': 'People want to talk about the new normal, but there isn’t one yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome. People talk about the new normal all the time now, but there isn’t one yet. There won’t be one for a long time to come. Our behavior is changing hourly with our moods, it seems, in response to stimuli that might be information, that might be instinct. It’s hard to say. We’re sitting at restaurant tables on the sidewalk, marching in the streets, streaming into thrift shops and bars. We’re giddy with pleasure, nervousness, joy, uncertainty. This person’s too close. That one’s too far.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/multimedia/17ah-newsletter-webtop/merlin_173472147_ba9f9602-874f-4b72-8286-024472d18138-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 870, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/17/multimedia/17ah-newsletter-webtop/merlin_173472147_ba9f9602-874f-4b72-8286-024472d18138-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 870}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/multimedia/17ah-newsletter-webtop/merlin_173472147_ba9f9602-874f-4b72-8286-024472d18138-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 707, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/multimedia/17ah-newsletter-webtop/merlin_173472147_ba9f9602-874f-4b72-8286-024472d18138-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1413, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/multimedia/17ah-newsletter-webtop/17ah-newsletter-webtop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/17/multimedia/17ah-newsletter-webtop/17ah-newsletter-webtop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/17/multimedia/17ah-newsletter-webtop/17ah-newsletter-webtop-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chance to Recharge Mentally, Spiritually and Emotionally', 'kicker': 'At Home Newsletter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-17T16:15:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'AtHome