', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lovia Gyarkye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lovia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gyarkye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d351df2c-8daa-5561-af23-db7f94aceca9', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d351df2c-8daa-5561-af23-db7f94aceca9'}, {'abstract': 'The singer-songwriter’s romance with June Carter is well-known, but this new documentary shines the spotlight on Cash’s first wife, Vivian Liberto.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/18/movies/my-darling-vivian-review.html', 'snippet': 'The singer-songwriter’s romance with June Carter is well-known, but this new documentary shines the spotlight on Cash’s first wife, Vivian Liberto.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mythologized version of the Johnny Cash story, his wife and collaborator, June Carter, is portrayed as the saintly woman who rescued the country singer from the dark side of fame. That story was immortalized in the 2005 film “Walk the Line,” for which Reese Witherspoon won the Oscar for best actress. Cash’s first wife, Vivian Liberto (played in that film by Ginnifer Goodwin), on the other hand, was made to look like a petty shrew on the sidelines when really she was the inspiration for the song “I Walk the Line.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18mydarling/merlin_173482677_b1c91817-16b8-4fc5-b4f1-dabf64eddd57-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18mydarling/merlin_173482677_b1c91817-16b8-4fc5-b4f1-dabf64eddd57-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18mydarling/merlin_173482677_b1c91817-16b8-4fc5-b4f1-dabf64eddd57-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18mydarling/merlin_173482677_b1c91817-16b8-4fc5-b4f1-dabf64eddd57-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1634, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18mydarling/18mydarling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18mydarling/18mydarling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18mydarling/18mydarling-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘My Darling Vivian’ Review: The Forgotten Wife of Johnny Cash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Darling Vivian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cash, Johnny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cash, June Carter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'My Darling Vivian (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liberto, Vivian (1934-2005)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riddlehoover, Matt (1985- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-18T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristen Yoonsoo Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristen', 'middlename': 'Yoonsoo', 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fbf626b-acf2-5265-8b67-2df59a80490c', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fbf626b-acf2-5265-8b67-2df59a80490c'}, {'abstract': 'A new HBO documentary looks at the man who helped send the director’s grandparents to their execution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/18/movies/bully-coward-victim-the-story-of-roy-cohn-review.html', 'snippet': 'A new HBO documentary looks at the man who helped send the director’s grandparents to their execution.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Bully. Coward. Victim.” is not the title you would expect for a documentary on Roy Cohn, the infamous Joseph McCarthy ally and Donald Trump mentor who built his name prosecuting Julius and Ethel Rosenberg. “Victim” seems especially perverse considering that the director, Ivy Meeropol, is a granddaughter of the Rosenbergs. The HBO film was originally scheduled to debut on Friday, the anniversary of their execution in 1953.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/bully1/bully1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/bully1/bully1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/bully1/bully1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/bully1/bully1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/bully1/bully1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/bully1/bully1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/bully1/bully1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bully. Coward. Victim.’ Review: The Paradox of Roy Cohn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'HBO Documentary Looks at Roy Cohn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meeropol, Ivy (1968- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'COHN, ROY MARCUS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bully. Coward. Victim. (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-18T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d839a8bf-bba2-51de-b3d4-fd25fcaaf40f', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d839a8bf-bba2-51de-b3d4-fd25fcaaf40f'}, {'abstract': 'The documentarians Yonatan Nir and Dani Menkin follow the nature photographer Amos Nachoum on his mission impossible: to capture a polar bear while swimming with it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/18/movies/picture-of-his-life-review.html', 'snippet': 'The documentarians Yonatan Nir and Dani Menkin follow the nature photographer Amos Nachoum on his mission impossible: to capture a polar bear while swimming with it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The underwater photographer Amos Nachoum’s white whale is no whale at all, but rather a polar bear. He’s swum with sharks, anacondas and crocodiles to capture stunning stills during his four-decade career, but never the Arctic predator. In fact, no one has ever shot the polar bear the way Nachoum wants to — while swimming with it — and for good reason: These animals consider humans part of their food chain, the cinematographer Adam Ravetch points out in the film.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18picture-art/merlin_173482869_541d6764-9828-4c3d-8d26-b3ebd26b6292-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18picture-art/merlin_173482869_541d6764-9828-4c3d-8d26-b3ebd26b6292-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18picture-art/merlin_173482869_541d6764-9828-4c3d-8d26-b3ebd26b6292-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/arts/18picture-art/merlin_173482869_541d6764-9828-4c3d-8d26-b3ebd26b6292-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_