d_count': 1372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2b7c6f5-8d71-5167-9db9-74b93de005a9'}, {'abstract': 'Her honest and empathic approach to changing white people and supporting black people is shifting perspectives on an increasingly large scale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/18/style/self-care/rachel-cargle-anti-racism-ally.html', 'snippet': 'Her honest and empathic approach to changing white people and supporting black people is shifting perspectives on an increasingly large scale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s lesson in the virtual classroom of Rachel Elizabeth Cargle, a public academic, writer, and lecturer, is “to give a more critical lens” for people “to view how they exist in the world.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-04/18juneteenth-promos-04-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-04/18juneteenth-promos-04-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 505}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-04/18juneteenth-promos-04-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-04/18juneteenth-promos-04-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1725, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-04/18juneteenth-promos-04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-04/18juneteenth-promos-04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-04/18juneteenth-promos-04-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Dear White Women’: The Public Classroom of Rachel Cargle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is Education', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juneteenth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cargle, Rachel Elizabeth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-selfcare', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-18T22:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'subsection_name': 'Self-Care', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siraad Dirshe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siraad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dirshe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6e309f7-2df9-564f-a292-e3718c4f3117', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6e309f7-2df9-564f-a292-e3718c4f3117'}, {'abstract': 'Aunt Jemima is retired, but real women lit a pathway to grace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/18/style/aunt-jemima-black-cooking.html', 'snippet': 'Aunt Jemima is retired, but real women lit a pathway to grace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was just five years old when the vibe in my grandmother Nannie’s kitchen aroused my culinary curiosity. It took 30 years and a dozen other hidden figures of the food world for me to appreciate the kitchen as a site for social change.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-02/18juneteenth-promos-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-02/18juneteenth-promos-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 505}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-02/18juneteenth-promos-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-02/18juneteenth-promos-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1725, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-02/18juneteenth-promos-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-02/18juneteenth-promos-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-02/18juneteenth-promos-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Women of the Jemima Code Freed Me', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is a Gift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Jemima Code: Two Centuries of African American Cookbooks (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-selfcare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juneteenth', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-18T22:15:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Tipton-Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tipton-Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad9c02ab-ae02-5e68-9f7a-a6f425581da3', 'word_count': 1445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad9c02ab-ae02-5e68-9f7a-a6f425581da3'}, {'abstract': 'In 1865, formerly enslaved people were promised 40 acres of land and, later, a mule. More than 150 years since then some politicians are trying to make good on a version of that promise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/18/us/politics/reparations-slavery.html', 'snippet': 'In 1865, formerly enslaved people were promised 40 acres of land and, later, a mule. More than 150 years since then some politicians are trying to make good on a version of that promise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Shaniyat Chowdhury, a Democratic candidate for Congress in New York, was asked about the most urgent concern facing his district, his options were not in short supply. He could have said housing or hunger. Healthcare was certainly on the table. But when prompted in a local news interview to name what he intends to do about his “single most pressing issue,” the 28-year-old democratic socialist had this answer: reparations, to address centuries of racial injustice.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-07/18juneteenth-promos-07-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-07/18juneteenth-promos-07-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 505}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-07/18juneteenth-promos-07-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-07/18juneteenth-promos-07-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1725, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-07/18juneteenth-promos-07-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/18/fashion/18juneteenth-promos-07/18juneteenth-promos-07-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 