ragraph': 'A year ago, Nicole Beharie never imagined that “Miss Juneteenth,” a small family drama celebrating African-American beauty and freedom, would be released just as another historic moment was unfolding. In fact, she hadn’t really considered Juneteenth — which honors the day the Emancipation Proclamation was read to slaves in Texas — at all before starring in the film. “I knew about the holiday, but I wasn’t celebrating it,” she admitted.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/19beharie1/19beharie1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/19beharie1/19beharie1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/19beharie1/19beharie1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/19beharie1/19beharie1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/19beharie1/19beharie1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/19beharie1/19beharie1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/19/arts/19beharie1/19beharie1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nicole Beharie on ‘Miss Juneteenth’ and the Danger of Labels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liberation and the Danger of Labels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Miss Juneteenth (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sleepy Hollow (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beharie, Nicole', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-19T14:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Candice Frederick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Candice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frederick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7f67954-10d1-515d-a44e-69e15b6394eb', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7f67954-10d1-515d-a44e-69e15b6394eb'}, {'abstract': 'The coronavirus disproportionately affects seniors, but they may not be included in important clinical trials for vaccines and treatments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/19/health/vaccine-trials-elderly.html', 'snippet': 'The coronavirus disproportionately affects seniors, but they may not be included in important clinical trials for vaccines and treatments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Picture the day — in six months, a year and a half or in 2023 — when university researchers or a pharmaceutical company announces a breakthrough against the virus that causes Covid-19.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/science/23SCI-NOAC