’s puzzle is one of those where the passage itself makes a great impression and recommends the book itself (we take brilliant cluing for granted with Team Cox/Rathvon, but not every end result is so vibrant). The book is “Curious Behavior,” by Robert R. Provine, and it concerns all manner of hiccups, yawns, sneezes and other reflexive emanations, including laughter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Acrostic', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Provine, Robert R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Emily (Crossword Constructor)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rathvon, Henry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-20T15:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2aa6605-0577-5729-8ca8-382d6072117a', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2aa6605-0577-5729-8ca8-382d6072117a'}, {'abstract': 'Father’s Day essays by Mike Birbiglia and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/20/parenting/fathers-day.html', 'snippet': 'Father’s Day essays by Mike Birbiglia and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tomorrow is Father’s Day! And we have three personal essays about fatherhood this week to help celebrate the dads in your life. There’s one from Kevin Powell, who has written a beautiful letter to the child he hopes to have. The piece is about how to survive in a world filled with fear, violence, sexism and racism. We have Mike Birbiglia, writing about how he, a sleepwalker, and his wife, J. Hope Stein, an insomniac, had a baby… who also didn\'t sleep. “There’s an expression, \'sleep like a baby,’ which I thought meant ‘deeply,’ but apparently means ‘doesn’t,’" Birbiglia writes. And we have Erik Vance, an NYT Parenting staff editor, telling us how he feared that fatherhood would make him lose his edge after spending his young adult life as a journalist, adventurer and explorer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/04/multimedia/04-parenting-nl/04-parenting-nl-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/04/multimedia/04-parenting-nl/04-parenting-nl-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/04/multimedia/04-parenting-nl/04-parenting-nl-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/04/multimedia/04-parenting-nl/04-parenting-nl-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/04/multimedia/04-parenting-nl/04-parenting-nl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/07/04/multimedia/04-parenting-nl/04-parenting-nl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/04/multimedia/04-parenting-nl/04-parenting-nl-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'c