es.com/2020/06/22/world/europe/china-eu-trade-talks.html', 'snippet': 'A first summit meeting between a new European leadership and China’s Xi Jinping yielded little, not even a joint statement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The European Union pleaded with Chinese leaders at a summit meeting Monday to put more effort into lagging negotiations on an investment and trade deal, an issue that has increasingly vexed the 27-member bloc. But the plea seemed likely to go unanswered by China, which has tightened control over its domestic economy and turned more combative in relations with Western powers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/world/22eu-china/merlin_173804388_2232ab4f-44f1-4aa8-8c65-5f4c35ce871e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/22/world/22eu-china/merlin_173804388_2232ab4f-44f1-4aa8-8c65-5f4c35ce871e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/world/22eu-china/merlin_173804388_2232ab4f-44f1-4aa8-8c65-5f4c35ce871e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/world/22eu-china/merlin_173804388_2232ab4f-44f1-4aa8-8c65-5f4c35ce871e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1303, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/world/22eu-china/22eu-china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/22/world/22eu-china/22eu-china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/world/22eu-china/22eu-china-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Betraying Frustration with China, E.U. Leaders Press for Progress on Trade Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.U. Leaders Press China on Trade Talks, With Scant Results', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-22T20:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a366fde-a303-50b0-aa08-e282e8283fa3', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a366fde-a303-50b0-aa08-e282e8283fa3'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists have linked historical political instability to a number of volcanic events, the latest involving an eruption in the Aleutian Islands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/22/science/rome-caesar-volcano.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists have linked historical political instability to a number of volcanic events, the latest involving an eruption in the Aleutian Islands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chaos and conflict roiled the Mediterranean in the first century B.C. Against a backdrop of famine, disease and the assassinations of Julius Caesar and other political leaders, the Roman Republic collapsed, and the Roman Empire rose in its place. Tumultuous social unrest no doubt contributed to that transition — politics can unhinge a society. But so can something arguably more powerful.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/30/science/22SCI-VOLCANO2/merlin_173804583_72bcec1a-97ae-4940-a96e-8b6231dfb66c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/30/science/22SCI-VOLCANO2/merlin_173804583_72bcec1a-97ae-4940-a96e-8b6231dfb66c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/30/science/22SCI-VOLCANO2/merlin_173804583_72bcec1a-97ae-4940-a96e-8b6231dfb66c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/30/science/22SCI-VOLCANO2/merlin_173804583_72bcec1a-97ae-4940-a96e-8b6231dfb66c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/30/science/22SCI-VOLCANO2/22SCI-VOLCANO2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/30/science/22SCI-VOLCANO2/22SCI-VOLCANO2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thum