'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolton, John R', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Demings, Val', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Kamala D', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-23T09:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins and Bret Stephens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stephens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/91a0725e-deac-59ef-b36a-cef94a9002f3', 'word_count': 1198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91a0725e-deac-59ef-b36a-cef94a9002f3'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview, the former national security said he accepted that he would pay a price for perhaps the most incriminating portrait of a president by such a high-level aide since the Watergate era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/23/us/politics/john-bolton-interview-trump.html', 'snippet': 'In an interview, the former national security said he accepted that he would pay a price for perhaps the most incriminating portrait of a president by such a high-level aide since the Watergate era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He knew what he was getting into. He knew he would be showered with brickbats from the left for not speaking out sooner and denounced by the right for speaking out at all. He knew he would be thrashed by thunderous presidential tweets, and he knew he might even be dragged into court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/us/politics/22dc-bolton/merlin_157114527_d286156b-50c3-4311-8598-3b0c7ee30aed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/22/us/politics/22dc-bolton/merlin_157114527_d286156b-50c3-4311-8598-3b0c7ee30aed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/us/politics/22dc-bolton/merlin_157114527_d286156b-50c3-4311-8598-3b0c7ee30aed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/us/politics/22dc-bolton/merlin_157114527_d286156b-50c3-4311-8598-3b0c7ee30aed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/us/politics/22dc-bolton/22dc-bolton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/22/us/politics/22dc-bolton/22dc-bolton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/us/politics/22dc-bolton/22dc-bolton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bolton Assaults Trump From the Right, and Takes Fire From All Directions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Always Outspoken, Bolton Is Comfortable With Scorn From All Sides', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolton, John R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Room Where It Happened: A White House Memoir (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-23T09:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e00565a6-8982-5b88-9e77-798444e2b417', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e00565a6-8982-5b88-9e77-798444e2b417'}, {'abstract': 'In a revolutionary summer, he may be losing the battle for the future of the left.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/23/opinion/bernie-sanders-protesters-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'In a revolutionary summer, he may be losing the battle for the future of the left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three months ago, Bernie Sanders lost his chance at the Democratic nomination, after a brief moment in which his socialist revolution seemed poised to raze the bastions of neoliberal power. But the developments of the last month, the George Floyd protests and their cultural repercussions, may prove the more significant defeat for the Sanders cause. In the winter he merely lost a presidential nomination; in the summer he may be losing the battle for the future of the left.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/merlin_170324484_7efdb4e4-a602-4dfb-89ed-14591a2ca5fc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/merlin_170324484_7efdb4e4-a602-4dfb-89ed-14591a2ca5fc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/merlin_170324484_7efdb4e4-a602-4dfb-89ed-14591a2ca5fc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/merlin_170324484_7efdb4e4-a602-4dfb-89ed-14591a2ca5fc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/23douthatWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/23douthatWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/23douthatWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Second Defeat of Bernie Sanders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Second Defeat of Bernie Sanders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Reform', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-23T09:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/017a3eda-87b1-5d5b-bb17-847ae601faf9', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/017a3eda-87b1-5d5b-bb17-847ae601faf9'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government’s spending on calamities related to global warming is a rapidly rising fiscal threat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/23/opinion/climate-change-financial-disaster.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government’s spending on calamities related to global warming is a rapidly rising fiscal threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The coronavirus crisis has forced the federal government to step up suddenly with fiscal stimulus to sustain the U.S. economy and help avoid a global depression. This necessary intervention comes at a price — a spike in federal debt that will need to be repaid over the long term. The resulting pressure on the government, U.S. taxpayers and the broader economy will intersect with another major fiscal challenge, one that we have yet to reckon with: climate change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23bodhar1/merlin_160189707_fa15f423-f0bc-4b35-b55b-72e5c47a44d2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23bodhar1/merlin_160189707_fa15f423-f0bc-4b35-b55b-72e5c47a44d2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23bodhar1/merlin_160189707_fa15f423-f0bc-4b35-b55b-72e5c47a44d2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23bodhar1/merlin_160189707_fa15f423-f0bc-4b35-b55b-72e5c47a44d2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23bodhar1/23bodhar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/23/opinion/23bodhar1/23bodhar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th