ank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic National Committee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-23T09:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shane Goldmacher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldmacher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44ea97a2-3966-566b-aab8-166506a90673', 'word_count': 1780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44ea97a2-3966-566b-aab8-166506a90673'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “The Biggest Bluff,” Maria Konnikova', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/23/books/review/the-biggest-bluff-maria-konnikova-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “The Biggest Bluff,” Maria Konnikova', 'lead_paragraph': 'The room is a sea of people. Bent heads, pensive faces, many obscured by sunglasses, hats, hoodies, massive headphones. It’s difficult to discern where the bodies end and the green of the card tables begins. Thousands of bodies sit in seeming disarray on chairs straight out of a seventies dining room catalogue—orange‐and‐mustard patterned upholstery, gold legs, vaguely square frame. Garish neon lights suspended on makeshift beams make the place look like the inside of a hospital that’s trying a bit too hard to appear festive. Everything is a bit worn, a bit out‐of‐date, a bit frayed. The only hints of deeper purpose are the color‐coded numbers hanging on strings from the ceiling. There’s the orange group, the yellow group, the white group. Each placard has a number and, beneath it, a picture of a single poker chip. The smell of stale casino air fills the room—old carpet; powder; a sweet, faintly sickly perfume; cold fried food and flat beer; and the unmistakable metallic tang of several thousand exhausted bodies that have been sharing the same space since morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Biggest Bluff,’ Maria Konnikova: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-06-23T09:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/383104e1-42b0-5aba-bc94-932f3dbb2ab4', 'word_count': 3179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/383104e1-42b0-5aba-bc94-932f3dbb2ab4'}, {'abstract': 'Two wallaroos and a red kangaroo were found dead in an outdoor exhibit days before a young mountain lion was captured in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/23/us/mountain-lion-san-francisco.html', 'snippet': 'Two wallaroos and a red kangaroo were found dead in an outdoor exhibit days before a young mountain lion was captured in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Officials at the San Francisco Zoo & Gardens are investigating whether a young mountain lion that was captured in the city last week was responsible for killing three marsupials in an outdoor exhibit at the zoo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/multimedia/22xp-zoo1/22xp-zoo1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/22/multimedia/22xp-zoo1/22xp-zoo1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth'