irement.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/opinion/sunday/InequalityIconsCh3-04/InequalityIconsCh3-04-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/26/opinion/sunday/InequalityIconsCh3-04/InequalityIconsCh3-04-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/opinion/sunday/InequalityIconsCh3-04/InequalityIconsCh3-04-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/opinion/sunday/InequalityIconsCh3-04/InequalityIconsCh3-04-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1131, 'width': 1648, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/opinion/sunday/InequalityIconsCh3-04/InequalityIconsCh3-04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/26/opinion/sunday/InequalityIconsCh3-04/InequalityIconsCh3-04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/opinion/sunday/InequalityIconsCh3-04/InequalityIconsCh3-04-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Future of Work Isn’t What People Think It Is', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Essential Labor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Domestic Workers Alliance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-24T09:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ai-jen Poo and Palak Shah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ai-jen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Palak', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b0c90ca-18cd-5d87-9b03-aae5d882cb3f', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b0c90ca-18cd-5d87-9b03-aae5d882cb3f'}, {'abstract': 'Many infections come from within. Doctors explain what they are and what to do about them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/24/parenting/virus-kids-sick-quarantine-infection.html', 'snippet': 'Many infections come from within. Doctors explain what they are and what to do about them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In April, about a month into a quarantine so careful I almost forgot how to drive, my 5-year-old came down with what I now refer to as “The Rash.” It started near her right eye, then spread down her right cheek — a red, menacing, puffy splotch. A few days later, it appeared on her left cheek, too. We arranged a telemedicine appointment with her pediatrician, who squinted at it and suggested it might be bacterial and ordered a round of topical and oral antibiotics. The medicines worked for as long as we had them: Exactly 48 hours after we stopped using them the splotches came back.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/multimedia/24parenting-getting-sick-hp/24parenting-getting-sick-hp-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/24/multimedia/24parenting-getting-sick-hp/24parenting-getting-sick-hp-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/multimedia/24parenting-getting-sick-hp/24parenting-getting-sick-hp-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/multimedia/24parenting-getting-sick-hp/24parenting-getting-sick-hp-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 800, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/multimedia/24parenting-getting-sick-hp/24parenting-getting-sick-hp-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/24/multimedia/24parenting-getting-sick-hp/24parenting-getting-sick-hp-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/multimedia/24parenting-getting-sick-hp/24parenting-getting-sick-hp-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Are My Kids Still Getting Sick in Lockdown?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Know That Children Can Still