ons, employees say a “systemic pattern of racial bias” permeates the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — Last week, Jeff Bezos, Amazon’s chief executive, wrote a rare note to all of the company’s employees. His leadership team had been reflecting on the “systemic racism” facing black communities, he said, and he urged employees to take time to learn and reflect on Juneteenth, the holiday marking the end of slavery in the United States.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/business/24unrest-amazon/merlin_164921967_30ec43c7-6969-408c-90d7-2af40e38a0a9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/24/business/24unrest-amazon/merlin_164921967_30ec43c7-6969-408c-90d7-2af40e38a0a9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/business/24unrest-amazon/merlin_164921967_30ec43c7-6969-408c-90d7-2af40e38a0a9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/business/24unrest-amazon/merlin_164921967_30ec43c7-6969-408c-90d7-2af40e38a0a9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/business/24unrest-amazon/00unrest-amazon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/24/business/24unrest-amazon/00unrest-amazon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {