irtually.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The roving project space We Buy Gold has turned to the painter Nina Chanel Abney to organize this online video exhibition of nearly a dozen artists who frame the body, most often black, in states of tension or rejuvenation, discomfort or grace. One above all commands attention: “Suspension,” a new work by the Johannesburg artist Thenjiwe Niki Nkosi, which stitches together archival footage of elite gymnasts into a seven-minute ode to personal and collective virtuosity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/arts/24virtual-galleries11/24virtual-galleries11-articleLarge.png', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/24/arts/24virtual-galleries11/24virtual-galleries11-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/arts/24virtual-galleries11/24virtual-galleries11-jumbo.png', 'height': 579, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/arts/24virtual-galleries11/24virtual-galleries11-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1157, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/24/arts/24virtual-galleries11/24virtual-galleries11-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/24/arts/24virtual-galleries11/24virtual-galleries11-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'capti