after the release of a video depicting the death of a handcuffed man. Three officers involved have already resigned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police chief of Tucson, Ariz., abruptly offered to resign on Wednesday while releasing a video in which a 27-year-old Latino man, Carlos Ingram Lopez, died in police custody two months ago. Mayor Regina Romero on Thursday expressed confidence in the police chief, Chris Magnus, and said he would stay on the job.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tucson Police in Turmoil After Death of Latino Man in Custody', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tucson Police in Turmoil Over Death of Handcuffed Latino Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Regina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tucson (Ariz)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Carlos Ingram (d 2020)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-24T22:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac42dcf3-fff0-558c-ad4e-b6851ecec442', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac42dcf3-fff0-558c-ad4e-b6851ecec442'}, {'abstract': 'Special Operations forces used a secret weapon designed to limit civilian casualties to strik