ytimes.com/2020/06/25/magazine/angelo-bassi-quantum-mechanic.html', 'snippet': 'For a century, quantum theory has been scientific orthodoxy. The Italian physicist Angelo Bassi is certain it isn’t the full story — and that he can prove it.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘The thing that amazes me is that quantum mechanics is only 100 years old,” the physicist Angelo Bassi said. We were in conversation across a picnic table on a drab Soviet-era campus in Zagreb, an early-autumn breeze swishing through the yellowing leaves of some nearby trees. “It’s a baby, it’s nothing — 100 years in the history of science. How can you just stop there? It doesn’t make sense any way you look at it.” We sat in the shadow of a rust-stained beige building where Bassi was about to speak at a workshop for physicists who specialize in the century-old subject.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-bassi/28mag-bassi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-bassi/28mag-bassi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-bassi/28mag-bassi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 839, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-bassi/28mag-bassi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1677, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-bassi/28mag-bassi-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-bassi/28mag-bassi-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-bassi/28mag-bassi-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rebel Physicist on the Hunt for a Better Story Than Quantum Mechanics', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Quantum Mechanic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bassi, Angelo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-25T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Henderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Henderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e1aedc1-bd79-5f01-893e-2bcb83b7eb29', 'word_count': 5651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e1aedc1-bd79-5f01-893e-2bcb83b7eb29'}, {'abstract': 'We’re being collected somewhere on video and in memory — and maybe we want to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/25/magazine/poem-surveillance.html', 'snippet': 'We’re being collected somewhere on video and in memory — and maybe we want to be.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Ganbatte” is Japanese for “hold out, persevere, do your best.” In the spring of 2020, those concepts took on new meaning for everyone — as did the concept of donning a ski mask and jumping through any door. Sarah Kortemeier’s poem from her mesmerizing debut collection, “Ganbatte,” offers a new twist on vigilance. We’re being collected somewhere on video and in memory, at all times, and maybe we want to be. Balcony waves are not quite enough. Selected by Naomi Shihab Nye', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-poem-1/28mag-poem-1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 220, 'width': 273, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-poem-1/28mag-poem-1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 220, 'width': 273, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-poem-1/28mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-poem-1/28mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-poem-1/28mag-poem-1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Surveillance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surveillance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-25T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kortemeier and Naomi Shihab Nye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kortemeier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': 'Shihab', 'lastname': 'Nye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6684517-1891-564b-a9c6-633e0799fb93', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6684517-1891-564b-a9c6-633e0799fb93'}, {'abstract': 'Her videos pull back the curtain on a president who, amid historic crises, has found almost nothing meaningful to say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/25/magazine/sarah-cooper-doesnt-mimic-trump-she-exposes-him.html', 'snippet': 'Her videos pull back the curtain on a president who, amid historic crises, has found almost nothing meaningful to say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Sarah Cooper lip-syncs Donald Trump’s news conferences, there’s no lectern or presidential seal. There’s no Mike Pence, face calibrated to Placid Gratitude as he gazes beatifically into the middle distance, and no Dr. Anthony Fauci, looking as though he’d give anything to be transported someplace better, like maybe Edvard Munch’s “The Scream.” No, in Cooper’s version there’s just Cooper, posting videos online, usually from her own apartment, miming along to the president’s characteristic rasp — part pontificating doorman, part tepid Marlon Brando impersonation, grasping from one excuse to another, one enemy to another, one wrecking ball to another.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-1/28mag-screenland-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 208, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-1/28mag-screenland-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 208}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-1/28mag-screenland-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-1/28mag-screenland-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 1700, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-1/28mag-screenland-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-1/28mag-screenland-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-1/28mag-screenland-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sarah Cooper Doesn’t Mimic Trump. She Exposes Him.', 'kicker': 'Screenland', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bit Part', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Senses and Sensation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-25T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By ZZ Packer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Packer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a9c4077-8aaa-548f-aefc-47b935511416', 'word_count': 1120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a9c4077-8aaa-548f-aefc-47b935511416'}, {'abstract': 'Why the great Russian novelist’s critique of state-sponsored violence bears thinking about now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/25/books/review/tolstoy-violence-war-and-peace-police.html', 'snippet': 'Why the great Russian novelist’s critique of state-sponsored violence bears thinking about now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early months of lockdown, many people stuck at home found themselves turning to unusual sources of comfort: Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s PowerPoint presentations, bread-baking (especially, for reasons unclear, sourdough) and “War and Peace,” Leo Tolstoy’s 1,200-page novel about the Napoleonic era in Russia.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/25Wilson/25Wilson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/25Wilson/25Wilson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/25Wilson/25Wilson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 921, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/25Wilson/25Wilson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 921, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/25Wilson/25Wilson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/25Wilson/25Wilson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/25Wilson/25Wilson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leo Tolstoy vs. the Police', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tolstoy vs. the Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Reform', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolstoy, Leo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Death of Ivan Ilyich (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'War and Peace (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-25T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28e69b7c-3367-5bc4-8d5e-374c71d126a7', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28e69b7c-3367-5bc4-8d5e-374c71d126a7'}, {'abstract': 'I wanted to let myself be swept away by the intoxicating fantasy of: What If?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/25/well/move/virtual-rowing-race-Oliver-Zeidler.html', 'snippet': 'I wanted to let myself be swept away by the intoxicating fantasy of: What If?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On June 11th, my 38th birthday, I found myself head-to-head in a virtual rowing race against the 23-year-old rowing champion Oliver Zeidler. Me, a father of two who has been rowing in his garage for three years, against Olli. Ridiculous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/well/00rowing/00rowing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/22/well/00rowing/00rowing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/well/00rowing/00rowing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/well/00rowing/00rowing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1324, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/well/00rowing/00rowing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/22/well/00rowing/00rowing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/22/well/00rowing/00rowing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Racing a World-Champion Rower in My Garage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rowing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2020)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-25T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Move', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Lukach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lukach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b626bc5-165c-5c8d-b4a3-a2cd965505ef', 'word_count': 1293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b626bc5-165c-5c8d-b4a3-a2cd965505ef'}, {'abstract': 'The best-selling author and former minority leader for the Georgia House of Representatives has a lot going on, but she still makes time for fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/25/books/review/our-time-is-now-stacey-abrams.html', 'snippet': 'The best-selling author and former minority leader for the Georgia House of Representatives has a lot going on, but she still makes time for fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOMAN OF WORDS The last thing Stacey Abrams, who is a Democrat, wanted to do was write a memoir about losing the 2018 Georgia gubernatorial race to the Republican, Brian Kemp. She says the idea came up, but “it was not appealing to me. As someone who has spent my adult life working on issues of access, justice and voting rights, I wanted to figure out, what could I say that was necessary? That told readers, here’s what we have to know, so history doesn’t repeat itself. I come from a family where our parents told us, if you see a problem, your job is to fix it. Writing is how I work through how to fix it.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/books/review/05insidethelist-web/merlin_169868115_9e016ff8-776b-4683-8d07-f437d4eeb07f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/05/books/review/05insidethelist-web/merlin_169868115_9e016ff8-776b-4683-8d07-f437d4eeb07f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/books/review/05insidethelist-web/merlin_169868115_9e016ff8-776b-4683-8d07-f437d4eeb07f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/books/review/05insidethelist-web/merlin_169868115_9e016ff8-776b-4683-8d07-f437d4eeb07f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/books/review/05insidethelist-web/05insidethelist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/07/05/books/review/05insidethelist-web/05insidethelist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/books/review/05ins