The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'School by Zoom might have been weird and compromised and unsatisfying, true. But now that it’s over and summer looms menacingly ahead with nothing but question marks for parents and kids — Is camp really safe? What about a job at the local mall or movie theater? What are we supposed to doooooo all day? — books are here to help. (Books are always here to help.) For the teens and tweens in my house, distraction has come lately by way of Jonathan Waldman and Rainbow Rowell and Pam Muñoz Ryan; for the parents and kids together, it’s come by way of nightly read-alouds from Philip Pullman’s “His Dark Materials” trilogy.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/books/25RecBooks/25RecBooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/25/books/25RecBooks/25RecBooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/books/25RecBooks/25RecBooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/books/25RecBooks/25RecBooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1372, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/books/25RecBooks/25RecBooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/25/books/25RecBooks/25RecBooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0,