Vaccine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Organizational', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-25T18:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Letters', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b40ebb1-f8e7-5d9a-8d1c-8d5cd7107120', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b40ebb1-f8e7-5d9a-8d1c-8d5cd7107120'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary style is eye-opening as it tests the boundaries of nonfiction filmmaking. Try “Crisis” and “Salesman” to start.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/25/movies/cinema-verite.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary style is eye-opening as it tests the boundaries of nonfiction filmmaking. Try “Crisis” and “Salesman” to start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a genre that ostensibly presents snippets of unvarnished truth, a particular type of documentary is difficult to name. The opening of “Chronicle of a Summer” (1961), a groundbreaking example by the anthropologist Jean Rouch and the sociologist Edgar Morin, calls it “cinéma vérité.” To the brothers Albert and David Maysles, it was “direct cinema.” Frederick Wiseman has used the phrase “reality fictions.” But in a 2015 interview, he told me he meant that term in jest: If Truman Capote could describe “In Cold Blood” as a nonfiction novel, then surely Wiseman could say his own films — shot unobtrusively, then edited with an eye toward characterization — added a novelistic spin to reality.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/arts/25gateway-verite3/merlin_173915904_aa492f09-e1d6-4a77-ae92-eadbdf9dfba3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/26/arts/25gateway-verite3/merlin_173915904_aa492f09-e1d6-4a77-ae92-eadbdf9dfba3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/arts/25gateway-verite3/merlin_173915904_aa492f09-e1d6-4a77-ae92-eadbdf9dfba3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/arts/25gateway-verite3/merlin_173915904_aa492f09-e1d6-4a77-ae92-eadbdf9dfba3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1477, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/arts/25gateway-verite3/25gateway-verite3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/26/arts/25gateway-verite3/25gateway-verite3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/26/arts/25gateway-verite3/25gateway-verite3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Cinéma Vérité Exist? Watch These 2 Movies to Find Out', 'kicker': 'Gateway Movies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unvarnished Truth, Give or Take a Few Edits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'n