 Haim add what was missing from previous releases — tension and texture —\xa0to make their sharpest and most adventurous songs yet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/26/arts/music/haim-women-in-music-pt-iii-review.html', 'snippet': 'On the band’s third album, the sisters in Haim add what was missing from previous releases — tension and texture —\xa0to make their sharpest and most adventurous songs yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Haim makes music of forward momentum, soundtracks for strutting confidently away from trouble. Its most memorable videos feature the trio’s members — the sisters Alana, Danielle and Este Haim — marching in loose lock step with one another, occasionally bursting into playful choreography. It’s a visual trope that lets them have some revisionist fun with girl group iconography, but it’s also a natural extension of their percussive sound. “We like rhythm,” Danielle said in a 2013 interview, after the release of their debut album, “Days Are Gone.” “It’s all these parts interlocking.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/27/arts/25ALBUM-HAIM1/merlin_173873709_2febc624-8587-4b40-a8a7-c26d33961372-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 487, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/27/arts/25ALBUM-HAIM1/merlin_173873709_2febc624-8587-4b40-a8a7-c26d33961372-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 487}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/27/arts/25ALBUM-HAIM1/merlin_173873709_2febc624-8587-4b40-a8a7-c26d33961372-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/27/arts/25ALBUM-HAIM1/merlin_173873709_2febc624-8587-4b40-a8a7-c26d33961372-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1664, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/27/arts/25ALBUM-HAIM1/25ALBUM-HAIM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/27/arts/25ALBUM-HAIM1/25ALBUM-HAIM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/27/arts/25ALBUM-HAIM1/25ALBUM-HAIM1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Haim Steps Into a New Groove on ‘Women in Music Pt. III’', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stepping Comfortably Into a New Groove', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haim (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haim, Alana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haim, Danielle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haim, Este', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Women in Music Pt III (Album)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-26T16:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Zoladz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zoladz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ba10b0f-e1f3-58c9-b985-7e99982e28ea', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ba10b0f-e1f3-58c9-b985-7e99982e28ea'}, {'abstract': 'This 30-minute dinner gets its crunch from pan-seared tofu, blistered snap peas and toasted cashews, and its flavor from an umami-rich sauce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/26/dining/tofu-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'This 30-minute dinner gets its crunch from pan-seared tofu, blistered snap peas and toasted cashews, and its flavor from an umami-rich sauce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tofu’s versatility is no secret, but to embrace its many uses is an exquisite thing — it can be pan-fried, grilled, blended into spreads and dressings, or tossed in a smoker for a few hours. Those who know tofu well understand it as an ingredient that is subtle and ever-so-slightly sweet, a willing canvas for flavors or a base for them to intermingle.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/26tofu1/merlin_172953354_f1b7e430-ff6a-4e61-917a-a79934af4d40-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/26tofu1/merlin_172953354_f1b7e430-ff6a-4e61-917a-a79934af4d40-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/26tofu1/merlin_172953354_f1b7e430-ff6a-4e61-917a-a79934af4d40-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/26tofu1/merlin_172953354_f1b7e430-ff6a-4e61-917a-a79934af4d40-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/26tofu1/26tofu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/26tofu1/26tofu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/26tofu1/26tofu1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This One-Pan Meal Shows Just How Joyful Tofu Can Be', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tofu Comes Alive As the Main Event', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tofu', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-26T16:08:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yewande Komolafe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yewande', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Komolafe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67484c7d-2d9b-559e-86c0-0a1b31133e1f', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67484c7d-2d9b-559e-86c0-0a1b31133e1f'}, {'abstract': 'With pubs and restaurants still closed in a country that has the world’s third-highest reported coronavirus death toll, crowds have flocked to beaches, parks and streams this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/26/world/europe/uk-coronavirus-lockdown.html', 'snippet': 'With pubs and restaurants still closed in a country that has the world’s third-highest reported coronavirus death toll, crowds have flocked to beaches, parks and streams this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — They descended by the tens of thousands on Britain’s southern beaches and jammed into city parks. They cavorted by the hundreds in streams. They attacked police officers who tried to disperse illegal block parties. And hundreds became stuck in mud flats while trying to reach the sea at low tide.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lockdown? What Lockdown? Heat Wave Brings Britons Out in Droves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britons, Sick of Lockdown, Boil Over in Summer Heat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Reopenings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-26T16:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ceylan Yeginsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ceylan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yeginsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/987d540a-d7a4-581a-8d48-7f8795479e24', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/987d540a-d7a4-581a-8d48-7f8795479e24'}, {'abstract': 'Readers variously praise Marty Goddard, a woman “who wanted to make a difference,” and say “the fight for survivors’ rights is one of attrition.”', 'web_url': 'https: