d', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bc86cc8-392c-534e-aef6-24f51a3f2e21', 'word_count': 1476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bc86cc8-392c-534e-aef6-24f51a3f2e21'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, June 27, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/26/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-a-conviction-vacated-but-only-after-a-25-year-prison-term.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, June 27, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Everyone in the criminal justice system failed you in some way or another.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: A Conviction Vacated, but Only After a 25-Year Prison Term', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-06-27T03:38:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fa9a191-55a1-524e-91e7-f6ce99ccc8d9', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fa9a191-55a1-524e-91e7-f6ce99ccc8d9'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Saturday, June 27, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/26/pageoneplus/corrections-june-27-2020.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Saturday, June 27, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A map with an article on May 31 about a clash in the Himalayas between India and China included outdated boundaries for Jammu and Kashmir. The India-controlled area just west of the Line of Actual Control is the territory of Ladakh, not Jammu and Kashmir.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: June 27, 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-06-27T03:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/595db21d-12c8-56c6-aba4-ee4f34bf344a', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/595db21d-12c8-56c6-aba4-ee4f34bf344a'}, {'abstract': 'Local tycoons and British-trained civil servants helped promote Beijing’s agenda in the territory. Now Beijing seems ready to push them aside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/27/world/asia/china-hong-kong.html', 'snippet': 'Local tycoons and British-trained civil servants helped promote Beijing’s agenda in the territory. Now Beijing seems ready to push them aside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s Communist Party has long pursued its agenda in Hong Kong by working through loyalists among the city’s top officials, lawmakers and tycoons. That behind-the-scenes approach was a key feature in preserving considerable autonomy for the territory.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/world/27hk-sidelined-1/merlin_173824485_ff4839de-a7d2-4918-95a4-01d87851acd9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/28/world/27hk-sidelined-1/merlin_173824485_ff4839de-a7d2-4918-95a4-01d87851acd9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/world/27hk-sidelined-1/merlin_173824485_ff4839de-a7d2-4918-95a4-01d87851acd9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '