d736e1f0e8d7'}, {'abstract': 'Many gig-based business models help customers take advantage of workers. Let’s stop giving tech companies a free ride.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/27/opinion/uber-covid-gig-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Many gig-based business models help customers take advantage of workers. Let’s stop giving tech companies a free ride.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The underpinning of countless Silicon Valley success stories is a method of commerce that treats millions of workers as disposable and deprives them of protections regular employees enjoy, like employer-paid health care. Keeping Uber drivers and DoorDash food couriers classified as contractors saves the companies billions in costs and has helped fuel billions more in investor value.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28uber_Sub/28uber_Sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28uber_Sub/28uber_Sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 679}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28uber_Sub/28uber_Sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 905, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28uber_Sub/28uber_Sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1809, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28uber_Sub/28uber_Sub-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': '