 {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-28T14:02:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Phillips', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Phillips', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d675238f-480a-525f-abc8-df80781ff4ca', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d675238f-480a-525f-abc8-df80781ff4ca'}, {'abstract': 'Make a vegan ranch dressing, from Superiority Burger in New York, and use it to top roasted potatoes, grilled romaine or even your next burger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/28/dining/what-to-cook-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Make a vegan ranch dressing, from Superiority Burger in New York, and use it to top roasted potatoes, grilled romaine or even your next burger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. A number of years ago, my friend and colleague Tejal Rao met up with a sous chef named Julia Goldberg at the vegetarian restaurant Superiority Burger in New York, where Goldberg then worked. Tejal had come to learn the secrets of one of Goldberg’s most elegant creations: A vegan ranch dressing (above), “tangy and creamy,” Tejal wrote for The Times, “turbocharged with the familiar mouth-smacking umami of bottled ranch.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28eat/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28eat/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28eat/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28eat/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28eat/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28eat/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28eat/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-06-28T14:40:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29371a57-f6c2-550d-9f6f-ea98e8bc0ae9', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29371a57-f6c2-550d-9f6f-ea98e8bc0ae9'}, {'abstract': 'The work of Hu Jie, who has made more than 30 movies, is little known even in China. The release of “Spark” and “The Observer” should make him better known abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/28/movies/hu-jie-films.html', 'snippet': 'The work of Hu Jie, who has made more than 30 movies, is little known even in China. The release of “Spark” and “The Observer” should make him better known abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than 20 years, the filmmaker Hu Jie has been trawling the deep waters of Chinese history to create a series of harrowing documentaries about the early years of Communist Party rule.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/00hu-jie-docs-observer/merlin_173631282_e635e940-7a9f-4037-bf74-c4fe6a61edb5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/00hu-jie-docs-observer/merlin_173631282_e635e940-7a9f-4037-bf74-c4fe6a61edb5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/00hu-jie-docs-observer/merlin_173631282_e635e940-7a9f-4037-bf74-c4fe6a61edb5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/00hu-jie-docs-observer/merlin_173631282_e635e940-7a9f-4037-bf74-c4fe6a61edb5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1635, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/00hu-jie-docs-observer/00hu-jie-docs-observer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/00hu-jie-docs-observer/00hu-jie-docs-observer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/00hu-jie-docs-observer/00hu-jie-docs-observer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Excavating Chinese History, One Harrowing Film at a Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘To Show Reality as It Really Was’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jie (Filmmaker)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Observer (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Searching for Lin Zhao's Soul (Movie)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Though I Am Gone (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Spark (2013) (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nanjing (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andreetti, Rita', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-28T14:43:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bc1a00f-7350-5944-a832-a4005d78db80', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bc1a00f-7350-5944-a832-a4005d78db80'}, {'abstract': 'History is repeating itself as pools, beaches and clubs open — but mostly for the privileged few.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/28/opinion/coronavirus-openings-summer-beaches.html', 'snippet': 'History is repeating itself as pools, beaches and clubs open — but mostly for the privileged few.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like other crises in the past, the coronavirus pandemic has provided an opportunity for communities to act on their most exclusionary impulses. This summer, private pools and beach clubs, as well as public facilities in wealthier areas, are reopening with new measures to ensure that the general public stays out: hiring more security, aggressively checking beach tags and restricting access to residents only.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/opinion/25kahrl2/merlin_172751712_3b5b022a-1efb-41e3-bb4c-6529c67f7949-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/25/opinion/25kahrl2/merlin_172751712_3b5b022a-1efb-41e3-bb4c-6529c67f7949-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/opinion/25kahrl2/merlin_172751712_3b5b022a-1efb-41e3-bb4c-6529c67f7949-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/opinion/25kahrl2/merlin_172751712_3b5b022a-1efb-41e3-bb4c-6529c67f7949-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/opinion/25kahrl2/25kahrl2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/25/opinion/25kahrl2/25kahrl2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/25/opinion/25kahrl2/25kahrl2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Will Get to Swim This Summer?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not All Will Get to Swim This Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-28T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew W. Kahrl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kahrl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c528275b-71a3-5302-baef-234c79f5778a', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c528275b-71a3-5302-baef-234c79f5778a'}, {'abstract': 'The state wanted to be among the first to reopen. It’s now dealing with the consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/28/opinion/texas-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'The state wanted to be among the first to reopen. It’s now dealing with the consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — For one brief, delusional moment in early April, I felt a smidgen of support for my governor, Greg Abbott. Sure, part of me thought his plan to reopen the state after just a few weeks of lockdown was cuckoo. Medical experts warned of a surge in coronavirus cases if Texas did just that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28swartz1/merlin_173601123_b462eba6-5515-47ad-a4b3-b2e9e3ea820c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28swartz1/merlin_173601123_b462eba6-5515-47ad-a4b3-b2e9e3ea820c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28swartz1/merlin_173601123_b462eba6-5515-47ad-a4b3-b2e9e3ea820c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/28/opinion/28swartz1/merlin_173601123_b462eba6-5515-47ad-a4b3-b2e9e3ea820c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1344, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 