ank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-29T22:04:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2396f0d3-1b5f-50c9-a58a-ba5aaa70b3b7', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2396f0d3-1b5f-50c9-a58a-ba5aaa70b3b7'}, {'abstract': 'Marky’s, a caviar dealer, now sells beluga raised in at an aquafarm in Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/29/dining/beluga-caviar.html', 'snippet': 'Marky’s, a caviar dealer, now sells beluga raised in at an aquafarm in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is not the best moment to discuss caviar, what with the pandemic and the subsequent fiscal stress. But there is some news worth noting: For the first time, beluga caviar, the roe of the largest variety of sturgeon, native to the Caspian Sea, has been successfully farm-raised in the United States. After 17 years of trying, Marky’s, a caviar producer, importer and dealer in Florida, has a crop of beluga from its Sturgeon Aquafarms in northern Florida. The importation, distribution and sale of purebred huso huso, or beluga, in the United States have been banned by the Fish & Wildlife Service since 2005, but this Marky’s caviar has been granted an exception to the ruling. So now, if you have $420 to splurge on a half-ounce, you can indulge in the delicate, buttery, nicely textured, though modest-grained, charcoal gray roe. And if a holiday in summer might not whet the appetite for jewel-box caviar, Marky’s also offers a celebratory package of American roes containing two ounces each of hackleback, paddlefish and salmon roes with blini and crème fraîche for $115 to enjoy on the Fourth.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-roe/29burner-roe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-roe/29burner-roe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-roe/29burner-roe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-roe/29burner-roe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1097, 'width': 1454, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-roe/29burner-roe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-roe/29burner-roe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-roe/29burner-roe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beluga, Farm-Raised in America', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Indulge: Farm-Raised Beluga Arrives From Florida', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caviar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sturgeon (Fish)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Marky's Caviar", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-29T22:22:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18d2e53b-ea5d-594f-a173-8ac00eb6e5b6', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18d2e53b-ea5d-594f-a173-8ac00eb6e5b6'}, {'abstract': 'Zimmerman, a pillar of the Nationals’ World Series-winning team, will skip the season, citing personal and family safety. Desmond of the Rockies, Joe Ross of the Nationals and Mike Leake of the Diamondbacks also opted out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/29/sports/baseball/ryan-zimmerman-nationals-opt-out.html', 'snippet': 'Zimmerman, a pillar of the Nationals’ World Series-winning team, will skip the season, citing personal and family safety. Desmond of the Rockies, Joe Ross of the Nationals and Mike Leake of the Diamondbacks also opted out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stories of the Washington Nationals and Ryan Zimmerman are intertwined. The franchise moved from Montreal, where they were known as the Expos, in 2005, the same year they drafted Zimmerman out of college. He reached the major leagues late that season and has been with them ever since, the face of the franchise through the lean seasons, their renaissance and, last year, their first World Series title.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/sports/29mlb-optout1/merlin_163379739_f3f1b6af-76eb-4f77-b6e8-ed332c9f1493-articleLarge.jpg', '