rticle', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By E. Tammy Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'E.', 'middlename': 'Tammy', 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ad369b1-dedf-54ba-a9c0-3251ff021580', 'word_count': 1224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ad369b1-dedf-54ba-a9c0-3251ff021580'}, {'abstract': 'An unreleased report commissioned by U.S. Special Operations Command found deficiencies in the military’s suicide-prevention programs for its elite troops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/30/magazine/special-operations-suicide-military.html', 'snippet': 'An unreleased report commissioned by U.S. Special Operations Command found deficiencies in the military’s suicide-prevention programs for its elite troops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He was one of the most elite military men in America, but his service in the Special Operations forces (S.O.F.) had taken a heavy toll. “The job I love and have committed my whole being to is creating my suicidal condition, but I’d rather die than admit to having trouble and being removed from my unit and my team,” he said often, according to someone close to him. It was impossible for The New York Times to follow up with this special operator, however, because he had died by suicide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/30/magazine/30atwar-sof-suicide/merlin_162798774_5b3e412b-9d24-4b30-8393-a72f832f4506-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/30/magazine/30atwar-sof-suicide/merlin_162798774_5b3e412b-9d24-4b30-8393-a72f832f4506-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':