m, “Hot Shot 2020,” is out July 10, puts roasted yam, street dancing and yacht parties in Jamaica on his list of must-haves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/30/arts/music/shaggy-jamaica-favorites.html', 'snippet': 'The reggae star, whose latest album, “Hot Shot 2020,” is out July 10, puts roasted yam, street dancing and yacht parties in Jamaica on his list of must-haves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty years ago, Shaggy released “Hot Shot” and kicked off a revolution: The dancehall album had two No. 1 hits on the Billboard Hot 100 chart, then “It Wasn’t Me” topped Britain’s singles chart; in the early 2000s, you could hear its sexy, infectious groove everywhere.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/arts/05my10-shaggy-web/05my10-shaggy-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/05/arts/05my10-shaggy-web/05my10-shaggy-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/arts/05my10-shaggy-web/05my10-shaggy-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/arts/05my10-shaggy-web/05my10-shaggy-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/arts/05my10-shaggy-web/05my10-shaggy-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/07/05/arts/05my10-shaggy-web/05my10-shaggy-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/05/arts/05my10-shaggy-web/05my10-shaggy-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Ask Shaggy to Touch the Mic at a Wedding', 'kicker': 'My Ten', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shaggy’s Must-Haves Usually Include Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaggy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica (West Indies)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reggae Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hot Shot 2020 (Album)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-30T14:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36419cff-cbe7-57b0-9ceb-b595f1b39e89', 'word_count': 1415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36419cff-cbe7-57b0-9ceb-b595f1b39e89'}, {'abstract': 'In this moment of polarization and racial justice, our critic looks back at Michael Moore’s smash documentary about the Iraq war and ‘The Notebook.’', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/30/movies/fahrenheit-911-movie-2004.html', 'snippet': 'In this moment of polarization and racial justice, our critic looks back at Michael Moore’s smash documentary about the Iraq war and ‘The Notebook.’', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last time the country was at war with itself, Michael Moore made a movie people were mad at, too. It opened at the end of June, 16 years ago. The parent-company that released it didn’t even want to. But after weeks of controversy, the Palme d’Or at Cannes and a very good trailer, Moore’s “Fahrenheit 9/11” had become a thing, such a thing that there was no not seeing it or, since we’re talking about scorched-earth culture combat, having feelings about its right to exist even if you hadn’t. By June 27, his documentary howl against the Iraq war earned him the No. 1 movie in North America.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/29morris-boxoffice-lead/29morris-boxoffice-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/29morris-boxoffice-lead/29morris-boxoffice-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/29morris-boxoffice-lead/29morris-boxoffice-lead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/29morris-boxoffice-lead/29morris-boxoffice-lead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/29morris-boxoffice-lead/29morris-boxoffice-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/29/arts/29morris-boxoffice-lead/29morris