 'byline': {'original': 'By Paige McClanahan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paige', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McClanahan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf7e52ea-24d6-5ca5-9c73-d58c88517aef', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf7e52ea-24d6-5ca5-9c73-d58c88517aef'}, {'abstract': 'Nneji in Astoria, Queens, from a Roosevelt Island market vendor, features a menu of comfort foods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/30/dining/nneji-astoria-queens.html', 'snippet': 'Nneji in Astoria, Queens, from a Roosevelt Island market vendor, features a menu of comfort foods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beatrice Ajaero grew up on Roosevelt Island, where she still lives, and has an African food and gift stall, Ibari, which she opened after obtaining a law degree and an M.B.A., in the Saturday market. Her new store, Nneji, in Astoria, Queens, has a limited menu, for takeaway, featuring West African red stew with chicken, peppery yassa with chicken, egusi melon seed and spinach soup with salmon, and a spinach and okra dish. Fonio, basmati rice and garri, which is cassava with a couscouslike texture, can be added. There are salads and occasional tagines. “I always wanted to share the tastes of my childhood,” said Ms. Ajaero, 29, whose family is Nigerian and who studied the Nigerian language Igbo, African history and political science. The name of the store means “mother” in Igbo.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-shop/29burner-shop-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-shop/29burner-shop-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-shop/29burner-shop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-shop/29burner-shop-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-shop/29burner-shop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-shop/29burner-shop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/dining/29burner-shop/29burner-shop-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Queens Shop Serves Nigerian Food', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Shop: Nigerian Food Is Focus Of Nneji in Queens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Astoria (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ajaero, Beatrice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nneji (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-06-30T14:53:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a29f9983-5542-5556-9f02-35f13d895728', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a29f9983-5542-5556-9f02-35f13d895728'}, {'abstract': 'Andy de Emmony directs this by-the-book adaptation of a children’s novel about a magical creature that can grant wishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/30/movies/four-kids-review.html', 'snippet': 'Andy de Emmony directs this by-the-book adaptation of a children’s novel about a magical creature that can grant wishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If a raggedy sand troll that grants children wishes feels like something out of a classic bedtime story, well, it is. The original conceit, by E. Nesbit, was published in 1902 as “Five Children and It,” and the children’s author Jacqueline Wilson updated the story in 2012 with “Four Children and It” to be about a blended family. Andy de Emmony’s film adapts the latter but has made the household mixed race, added teen angst and wrapped it all into a dull, family-friendly package.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/arts/30fourkids/merlin_173961567_761e4beb-a2ba-4db5-9521-8bfd700efece-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 242, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/01/arts/30fourkids/merlin_173961567_761e4beb-a2ba-4db5-9521-8bfd700efece-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 242}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/arts/30fourkids/merlin_173961567_761e4beb-a2ba-4db5-9521-8bfd700efece-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/01/arts/30fourkids/merlin_173961567_761e4beb-a2ba-4db