organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eb7c518-f118-5337-a822-ee9b42bf243e', 'word_count': 1415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eb7c518-f118-5337-a822-ee9b42bf243e'}, {'abstract': 'With her legs paralyzed, she found freedom rowing across oceans. “It’s hopeless, it’s majestic, it’s exhilarating,” she said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/30/sports/olympics/angela-madsen-paralympian-dead.html', 'snippet': 'With her legs paralyzed, she found freedom rowing across oceans. “It’s hopeless, it’s majestic, it’s exhilarating,” she said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angela Madsen was a healthy young Marine who was playing basketball when she suffered a serious back injury in 1981. When she had back surgery a dozen years later, at 33, she woke up paralyzed from the waist down. She lost her job, her partner cleaned out her bank account and left her, and for a time she lived on the streets, sleeping in her wheelchair in front of Disneyland.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/02/obituaries/26Madsen1/merlin_173896500_6778b9b7-355d-40af-8f01-777d7e0141ac-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/02/obituaries/26Madsen1/merlin_173896500_6778b9b7-355d-40af-8f01-777d7e0141ac-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/02/obituaries/26Madsen1/merlin_173896500_6778b9b7-355d-40af-8f01-777d7e0141ac-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/02/obituaries/26Madsen1/merlin_173896500_6778b9b7-3